abstract: >-
  Lecture materials on machine learning interpretability for SCC5819 Topics
  in Artificial Intelligence, a graduate course at ICMC-USP taught by
  Prof. Andre Carlos Ponce de Leon Ferreira de Carvalho, following
  Christoph Molnar's Interpretable Machine Learning. Module 00 acquires,
  treats and documents the SRAG/SIVEP-Gripe surveillance base (Brazil,
  2019-2024), defines a retrospective outcome task in the recorded
  hospitalized COVID cohort and documents the historical model selection.
  Each method pairs an executed lecture notebook with a technical companion
  that checks the computation and declares its scope. The modules share the
  reference predictor and temporal split; exemplars, panels and background
  samples are chosen for each explanation task. The sequence covers ceteris
  paribus profiles (01),
  individual conditional expectation curves (02), LIME (03, including a
  line-by-line validation of the lime package internals), counterfactual
  explanations (04), SHAP (05), partial dependence (06), accumulated local
  effects (07), pairwise feature interaction (08), decomposition of a joint
  partial-dependence surface (09) and permutation feature importance (10).
